# .governance/.gitignore
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file defines which governance artifacts are local/volatile and should
# NOT be tracked in version control.
#
# Policy Owner: Repository Governance Owner
# Last Updated: 2026-07-04
# Related: REPOSITORY_GOVERNANCE.md, docs/decisions/README.md
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Local Performance & Legacy Manifests ──────────────────────────────────────
# manifest.local.json was generated by an older AuditEngine implementation that
# split volatile performance stats into a separate file. The current engine
# consolidates all metadata into manifest.json (with volatility filtering).
# This file is a dead leftover artifact and should never be committed.
manifest.local.json

# ── Local Session & Analytics Data ────────────────────────────────────────────
# analytics/ is written by the governance AnalyticsStore to track local fixing
# sessions (sessions.json, fixes.json, rules.json, trends.json).
# These files are machine-specific and not consumed by any validator, CI gate,
# or application code. They are purely local developer tooling output.
analytics/

# ── Daily Archive Snapshots ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# archive/history/ contains daily date-keyed snapshots (e.g. 2026-07-04.json).
# These are generated by the audit engine to support local trend analysis.
# They are not part of the canonical governance baseline and should not be
# committed — snapshot trends are captured in metrics/trend-metrics.json instead.
archive/
